  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "none noted",
    "relation": "tests",
    "tranche": "T3",
    "tranche_reason": "The study measures downstream math-task accuracy across model sizes and describes the resulting curves, rather than measuring held-out language-modeling loss as in the original scaling-law studies.",
    "gate_note": "The study reports GSM8K accuracy curves and accuracy results on four math datasets for FlanT5 models before and after specialization; these bear on V6. It does not measure held-out pretraining loss, tokens, or training compute. Checkpoint dynamics and the model-selection comparison concern training stage or selection choice rather than a scale-performance relation, so they are not recorded as rows.",
    "test_reason": "The study reports downstream math accuracy across T5/FlanT5 sizes (250M–11B), before and after specialization by distillation fine-tuning. It describes the curves as log-linear in model scale. That is a new-setting result bearing on V6. It does not measure pretraining loss.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly right. The authors also argue that, because specialized small models show log-linear curves like large models, chain-of-thought may not be an emergent ability. They recommend instruction-tuned starting checkpoints, and they report tradeoffs: BBH loss, in-distribution vs OOD, and in-context vs zero-shot.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "Uses downstream math-task accuracy rather than held-out language-modeling loss; evaluates fine-tuned/specialized models and does not sweep training tokens or compute.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Specialization changes the accuracy curve; results also differ by dataset, including a decrease for the 11B FlanT5 on SVAMP.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Distillation-based specialization on GSM8K raises math accuracy by about +10 for small FlanT5 models while largely erasing BBH ability.",
        "proposed_claim": "Task-specific fine-tuning shifts the downstream scaling curve upward at the cost of generic ability.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r1",
          "r2",
          "r3",
          "r4",
